        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If the stone works for a living — countertops, floors, patios, showers — it wants an impregnating sealer, and it wants one because vapour has to get out and films do not survive being used.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Topical sealers earn their place where appearance is the objective and the stone is dry on all sides. Everywhere else, a colour-enhancing impregnator gets you most of the look without the peeling, which is why it has quietly become the standard answer outdoors.
          </p>
